  "name": "CATECHOLAMINES  BLOOD",
  "code": "1052",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Normal Results:</strong></span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Catecholamines within reference ranges indicate no evidence of catecholamine-secreting tumor or acute sympathetic overactivity<span class=\"whitespace-nowrap\">.</span></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Elevated Catecholamines:</strong></span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Can be associated with:</span></p>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Pheochromocytoma or paraganglioma (adrenal tumors)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Neuroblastoma (in pediatric cases)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Acute stress or anxiety</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Severe illness, hypoglycemia, strenuous exercise, or certain medications</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Low Results:</strong></span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Usually of little clinical concern; extremely low values may require correlation with clinical setting.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
